NAME: Altitude

DESCRIPTION:

Displays and graphs altitude.

Newer devices provide altitude in feet
above Mean Sea Level (MSL).

Older devices provide altitude in feet
above the the WGS84 ellipsoid (WGS84).

NOTES:

Permission to access fine location must 
be granted.

The Altitude app relies on altitude data
that is saved in 
  svcs/Altitude/altitude.dat, 
by the Altitude service. The altitude.
dat stores hourly altitude data, and 
supports storing altitude data from year
2026 to 2045.

The Altitude service obtains altitude 
data from GPS. GPS altitude raw readings
are based on the WGS84 ellipsoid, not
mean sea level. EzApp uses the Android
AltitudeConverter to convert the WGS84 
values to mean sea level.

Even when using the AltitudeConverter, 
to convert the raw GPS to MSL, the 
altitude can be off by 150 feet.
